{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2020-05-07 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': '3M Awarded Department Of Defense Contracts To Further Expand U.S. Production Of N95 Respirators', 'text': "3M AWARDED DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE CONTRACTS TO FURTHER EXPAND U.S. PRODUCTION OF N95 RESPIRATORS.WILL INCREASE U.S. PRODUCTION FROM 35 MLN PER MONTH TO MORE THAN 95 MLN PER MONTH BY OCTOBER.HAS BEEN AWARDED TWO CONTRACTS THROUGH U.S. DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE IN RECENT WEEKS TO FURTHER EXPAND U.S. PRODUCTION OF N95 RESPIRATORS .INVESTED OVER $80 MLN IN RAMPING UP N95 RESPIRATOR PRODUCTION SINCE OUTBREAK BEGAN IN JANUARY.WORKING WITH TRUMP ADMINISTRATION TO IMPORT 166.5 MLN RESPIRATORS FROM 3M'S OVERSEAS MANUFACTURING FACILITIES IN CHINA & OTHER ASIA LOCATIONS.IMPORTS OF RESPIRATORS HAVE ALREADY BEGUN AND WILL CONTINUE OVER COMING MONTHS.CONSTRUCTION OF EQUIPMENT HAS BEGUN IN WISCONSIN WHERE INITIAL PRODUCTION OF RESPIRATORS WILL START IN JUNE.EQUIPMENT WILL EVENTUALLY BE RELOCATED TO A NEW EXPANSION AT 3M'S FACILITY IN ABERDEEN, SOUTH DAKOTA."}{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2020-05-07 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Abbvie Says Allergan CEO Brent Saunders Has Elected Not To Join Abbvie Board', 'text': "ABBVIE INC - ALLERGAN'S CURRENT CHAIRMAN AND CEO BRENT SAUNDERS HAS ELECTED NOT TO JOIN ABBVIE BOARD."}{'symbol': 'AES', 'date': '2020-05-07 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AES Reports Q1 Adj EPS Of $0.29', 'text': 'Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.29.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.22.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.29 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPECTS A LIMITED NEAR-TERM IMPACT FROM COVID-19 PANDEMIC.EXPECTS TO COMFORTABLY EXCEED TARGETED INVESTMENT GRADE RATIO OF PARENT FREE CASH FLOW TO RECOURSE DEBT AT YEAR-END 2020.REDUCING MID-POINT OF 2020 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE BY 5%, OR $0.07 PER SHARE.REAFFIRMING 7% TO 9% AVERAGE ANNUAL GROWTH TARGET FOR ADJUSTED EPS AND PARENT FREE CASH FLOW THROUGH 2022.REMAIN COMMITTED TO GROWING DIVIDEND BY 4% TO 6% ANNUALLY.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE $2.34 BILLION VERSUS $2.65 BILLION.'}{'symbol': 'ALB', 'date': '2020-05-07 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Albemarle Reports Q1 Adjusted Earnings Per Share $1.00', 'text': 'ALBEMARLE REPORTS FIRST QUARTER RESULTS.Q1 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.00.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.01.Q1 SALES $739 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $762.3 MILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.83 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ACCELERATING $100 MILLION COST SAVINGS INITIATIVE.NOW EXPECT TO REALIZE BETWEEN $50 AND $70 MILLION OF COST SAVINGS IN 2020.REDUCING 2020 CAPITAL SPENDING BY ABOUT $150 MILLION FROM PLAN.IMPLEMENTING SHORT-TERM CASH MANAGEMENT ACTIONS TO SAVE BETWEEN $25 AND $40 MILLION PER QUARTER.WITHDRAWING FULL-YEAR 2020 OUTLOOK.ANTICIPATES THAT Q2 PERFORMANCE WILL BE LOWER YEAR-OVER-YEAR BASED ON REDUCED GLOBAL ECONOMIC ACTIVITY DUE TO GLOBAL PANDEMIC.SEES Q2 NET SALES $700 - $775 MILLION.SEES Q2 ADJUSTED EBITDA $140 - $190 MILLION.Q2 REVENUE VIEW $767.5 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.TO DATE, CO HAS EXPERIENCED MINIMAL ORDER REDUCTIONS..CUSTOMER CLOSURES AND ORDER CANCELLATIONS ARE LIKELY TO AFFECT SPECIALTY AND TECHNICAL GRADE PRODUCTS IN Q2.CONTINUE TO SEE SOLID BATTERY GRADE ORDERS IN Q2 2020 AS BATTERY MANUFACTURERS CATCH UP ON BACKLOG ORDERS PLACED PRIOR TO COVID-19.IMPACT OF RECENT AUTOMOTIVE OEM SHUTDOWNS IS EXPECTED TO BE DELAYED INTO H2 2020..TO DATE, BROMINE DEMAND HAS REMAINED RELATIVELY STRONG.FUTURE BROMINE DEMAND IS LIKELY TO BE IMPACTED BY RECENT COVID-19 SHUT-DOWNS.'}{'symbol': 'ALXN', 'date': '2020-05-07 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alexion Pharmaceuticals Sees FY Revenue $5,230 Mln To $5,330 Mln', 'text': 'ALEXION REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.22.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.50.Q1 REVENUE $1.445 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.36 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.71 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPLORING POTENTIAL ROLE OF ULTOMIRIS AND SOLIRIS FOR TREATMENT OF SEVERE COVID-19.RECENTLY INITIATED A PHASE 3 RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED TRIAL OF ULTOMIRIS IN A SUBSET OF ADULTS WITH COVID-19.ALSO DONATED SUPPLY OF SOLIRIS FOR COMPASSIONATE USE AND EXPANDED ACCESS PROGRAMS..GUIDANCE ASSUMES A GRADUAL RE-OPENING OF HEALTHCARE SYSTEM ACCESS STARTING IN JULY..COMMITTED TO CONTINUING CLINICAL TRIALS WITH AS LITTLE INTERRUPTION AS POSSIBLE.EXPECT THERE WILL BE LITTLE TIMING IMPACT ON FULLY-ENROLLED TRIALS.EXPECT TIMING SHIFT OF AT LEAST THREE MONTHS ON TRIALS THAT ARE ENROLLING PATIENTS AND ACTIVATING SITES.ALL HEALTHY VOLUNTEER STUDIES HAVE BEEN TEMPORARILY PAUSED..SEEN INITIAL SIGNS OF SLOWING NEW PATIENT INITIATIONS AND DELAYS IN TREATMENT STARTS.DECREASING FY TOTAL REVENUES AND EPS GUIDANCE AND INCREASING NON-GAAP OPERATING MARGIN GUIDANCE.SEES FY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $10.45 TO $10.75.SEES FY EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.14 TO $8.47.SEES FY REVENUE $5,230 TO $5,330 MILLION.SEES FY SOLIRIS/ULTOMIRIS REVENUES $4,495 TO $4,570 MILLION.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $10.97, REVENUE VIEW $5.61 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'GOOGL', 'date': '2020-05-07 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lime Says Uber Leading $170 Million Investment Round With Participation From Alphabet, Bain Capital Ventures, Gv And Other Existing And New Investors', 'text': ':LIME SAYS UBER LEADING $170 MILLION INVESTMENT ROUND WITH PARTICIPATION FROM ALPHABET, BAIN CAPITAL VENTURES, GV AND OTHER EXISTING AND NEW INVESTORS.LIME SAYS AS PART OF THE INVESTMENT, CO HAS ACQUIRED JUMP’S BUSINESS OPERATIONS AND WILL FURTHER EXPAND ITS MOBILE APP INTEGRATION WITH UBER.'}{'symbol': 'GOOGL', 'date': '2020-05-07 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ViacomCBS And Google Expand Distribution Deal To Deliver More ViacomCBS Content On YouTube TV', 'text': 'VIACOMCBS AND GOOGLE EXPAND DISTRIBUTION DEAL TO DELIVER MORE VIACOMCBS CONTENT ON YOUTUBE TV – COMPANIES.VIACOMCBS - DEAL INCLUDES CONTINUED COMMITMENT TO DISTRIBUTE CO’ PREMIUM SUBSCRIPTION SERVICES, INCLUDING SHOWTIME, ON YOUTUBE TV.VIACOMCBS - MULTI-YEAR, EXPANDED AGREEMENT INTRODUCES 14 VIACOMCBS CHANNELS TO LIVE TV, ON-DEMAND SUBSCRIPTION SERVICE.VIACOMCBS - FINANCIAL TERMS OF THE AGREEMENT WERE NOT DISCLOSED.'}{'symbol': 'AAL', 'date': '2020-05-07 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': "UK's CMA Says BA, American Airlines Offer Commitments On Competition Concerns Over Airline Routes", 'text': 'BRITISH AIRWAYS, AMERICAN AIRLINES OFFERED COMMITMENTS TO RESOLVE COMPETITION CONCERNS OVER AGREEMENT ABOUT AIRLINE ROUTES BETWEEN UK, US.BRITISH AIRWAYS, AMERICAN AIRLINES TO MAKE SLOTS AVAILABLE AT LONDON HEATHROW OR GATWICK AIRPORTS TO RESOLVE COMPETITION CONCERNS.BA, AMERICAN AIRLINES RELEASING EXTRA SLOTS TO LET COMPETITORS BEGIN OR INCREASE NON-STOP FLIGHTS BETWEEN LONDON & BOSTON, DALLAS & MIAMI.PROCEEDING TO MARKET TEST PROPOSED PACKAGE BY BA, AMERICAN AIRLINES BUT ALSO GIVING EXTRA TIME FOR RESPONSES IF NEEDED.'}{'symbol': 'AWK', 'date': '2020-05-07 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Water Works Reports Q1 Adjusted Non-GAAP EPS Of $0.67', 'text': 'AMERICAN WATER REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.SEES FY 2020 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.85 TO $3.95.Q1 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.67.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.68.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.65 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.79 TO $3.89 EXCLUDING ITEMS.FY2020 REVENUE VIEW $3.79 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.BOARD APPROVED A 10% INCREASE IN QUARTERLY DIVIDEND TO 55 CENTS PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'AMP', 'date': '2020-05-07 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ameriprise Financial Increases Regular Quarterly Dividend', 'text': "AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL INCREASES REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND.AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL INC - INCREASED COMPANY'S QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND BY 7 PERCENT, OR $0.07 PER DILUTED SHARE, TO $1.04 PER DILUTED SHARE."}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2020-05-07 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Amerisourcebergen Sees 2020 Rev Growth In Low- To Mid-Single Digit Percent Range', 'text': 'AMERISOURCEBERGEN REPORTS FISCAL 2020 SECOND QUARTER RESULTS.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $7.35 TO $7.65.Q2 ADJUSTED EA